WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.777
A Pluto investigation is saved Julia
source that you can edit.

00:00:03.777 --> 00:00:07.372
Expand a cell, change its code, and submit
it to update the

00:00:07.372 --> 00:00:11.271
reactive output. Pluto saves the cell back
to the notebook file.

00:00:11.402 --> 00:00:14.728
That source save is separate from Save
completed reports,

00:00:14.728 --> 00:00:18.054
which retains finished suite evidence.
Keep both when you

00:00:18.054 --> 00:00:21.263
want an editable investigation and a
measured baseline.

00:00:21.395 --> 00:00:25.100
Use Open Pluto notebook to resume the
saved file. Reopening

00:00:25.100 --> 00:00:28.554
an active notebook reveals its existing
tab and server.

00:00:28.554 --> 00:00:32.071
After a stopped session, the saved source
is used again.

00:00:32.202 --> 00:00:35.837
Selecting a different check does not
silently request another

00:00:35.837 --> 00:00:39.412
measurement. For checks, use the explicit
Launch, Cancel and

00:00:39.412 --> 00:00:43.166
Refresh controls. For source edits, use
Pluto's reactive cells.

00:00:43.297 --> 00:00:46.414
This separation lets you explore the
explanation while

00:00:46.414 --> 00:00:49.589
retaining control over the experiment you
actually run.
